lset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WGYuoDv7w93eZ8kcnJheD2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` was using `ROUND_HALF_UP` (despite its docstring).\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, `round_money` now uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. The first attempt to open it failed with a temporary server error (503). I confirmed no PR had been created, then retried with the same request key so it couldn't open twice.\n\nI haven't merged it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}